## Implemented in the testing branch

- Independent dashboard switches and configurable radius.
- Backward-compatible GeoJSON points and geospatial indexes.
- Share/update/remove location controls in one location screen.
- Mutual Nearby People matching, stable partitioning, and `📍` marker.
- Optional local setting on the final discussion preview.
- Fixed creator-location snapshots on local discussions.
- Nearby-first Local Discussion discovery with stable existing ranking.
- Privacy-safe rendering, strict coordinate validation, focused tests, integration tests, and source-of-truth docs.

## Follow-up before rollout

1. Manually test and polish Persian and English wording.
2. Decide whether an already-created discussion may add/remove its local status.
3. Add privacy-safe adoption/conversion analytics before a measured rollout.
4. Add aggregate dashboard counts for location-sharing discoverable users and local discussions if needed for rollout decisions.
5. Run a real Mongo geospatial smoke test with accounts just below and exactly at the configured radius.
6. Deploy with both switches off and enable only after the manual privacy/UX review.
